-- title:
--   Regularity of the special fibre at ∞-Igusa cusps
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \ge 5$, let $M' \ge 1$ be a natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ and admitting a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L(\!(X)\!)/L$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$, where $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ is the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ its fraction field, with $q$ in the maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and with a compatible $A$-algebra structure on $K$; let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j \in K$ be the element whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant, assumed nonzero. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ characterised by: $f \in W_0$ precisely when there are power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $f \cdot y = x$ in $L(\!(X)\!)$ after applying $A \to L$ coefficientwise (the Gauss valuation ring of $A$-integral $q$-expansions). Let $\mathfrak{X} = \mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}(A, K, j)$ be the pushout of the two inclusions of charts, the charts being the integral closures of $A[j]$ and of $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$, and let $z \in \mathfrak{X}$ be a point. Write $\varpi_z$ for the germ at $z$ of the global section of $\mathfrak{X}$ obtained from $\varpi$ along the structure morphism [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L258) to $\operatorname{Spec} A$, and assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z$. Assume further that $z$ is not in the image of the finite chart $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A[j]$ under [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.ιFin`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L238), and that for every prime $y$ of the integral closure of $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$ mapping to $z$ under [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.ιInf`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L240), every element of that chart whose image in $K$ is a nonunit of $W_0$ lies in $y$. Then the quotient of the stalk of $\mathfrak{X}$ at $z$ by the ideal generated by $\varpi_z$ is a regular local ring.
--
--   This is the regularity of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X(\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M'))$ over $A$ at those points of the cuspidal locus (points where $j$ has a pole) that lie on the Igusa component through $\infty$, singled out here by the condition that the nonunits of the Gauss valuation ring $W_0$ are contained in the prime under $z$ on the $j^{-1}$-chart. It feeds the construction of an open subscheme of the integral model that is smooth over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and the corresponding statement of regularity of the special fibre at good points.
